      "answer": "$17/28=0.607$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Method 1 — classify selections by the numbers of 2s, 4s and digits from $1,3,5$.\n\nNumber of 2s; Number of 4s; Number from $1,3,5$; Calculation; Ways\n0; 0; 3; ${3\\choose3}$; 1\n0; 1; 2; ${3\\choose1}{3\\choose2}$; 9\n1; 0; 2; ${2\\choose1}{3\\choose2}$; 6\n1; 1; 1; ${2\\choose1}{3\\choose1}{3\\choose1}$; 18\n\nTotal favourable selections $=34$. Total selections $={8\\choose3}=56$. Probability $=34/56=17/28=0.607$.\n\nM1: One correct unsimplified calculation for an identified scenario containing 1 and 2 and/or 1 and 4.\n\nA1: Two correct outcomes evaluated. Accept unsimplified.\n\nM1: Four correct scenarios added.\n\nB1: ${8\\choose3}$ or 56 used as the denominator of a probability expression.\n\nA1: $17/28$ or 0.607.\n\nMethod 2 — enumerate the ten sets of three different values.\n\nValues; Calculation; Ways\n1,2,3; ${1\\choose1}{2\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 2\n1,2,4; ${1\\choose1}{2\\choose1}{3\\choose1}$; 6\n1,2,5; ${1\\choose1}{2\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 2\n1,3,4; ${1\\choose1}{1\\choose1}{3\\choose1}$; 3\n1,3,5; ${1\\choose1}{1\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 1\n1,4,5; ${1\\choose1}{3\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 3\n2,3,4; ${2\\choose1}{1\\choose1}{3\\choose1}$; 6\n2,3,5; ${2\\choose1}{1\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 2\n2,4,5; ${2\\choose1}{3\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 6\n3,4,5; ${1\\choose1}{3\\choose1}{1\\choose1}$; 3\n\nTotal favourable selections $=34$; denominator ${8\\choose3}=56$; probability $=17/28=0.607$.\n\n(M1): One correct unsimplified calculation for an identified scenario containing 1 and 2 and/or 1 and 4.\n\n(A1): Five correct outcomes evaluated. Accept unsimplified.\n\n(M1): Ten correct scenarios added.\n\n(B1): ${8\\choose3}$ or 56 used as the denominator of a probability expression.\n\n(A1): $17/28$ or 0.607.\n\nMethod 3 — ordered selections.\n\nThe ordered favourable numerators over $8\\times7\\times6=336$ are: 1,2,3: 12; 1,2,4: 36; 1,2,5: 12; 1,3,4: 18; 1,3,5: 6; 1,4,5: 18; 2,3,4: 36; 2,3,5: 12; 2,4,5: 36; 3,4,5: 18. Their sum is 204, so the probability is $204/336=17/28=0.607$.\n\n(M1): One correct unsimplified ordered calculation for an identified scenario containing 1 and 2 and/or 1 and 4.\n\n(A1): Five correct outcomes evaluated. Accept unsimplified.\n\n(M1): Ten correct scenarios added.\n\n(B1): 336 or $8\\times7\\times6$ used as the denominator.\n\n(A1): $17/28$ or 0.607.\n\nMethod 4 — subtract selections containing repeated values from all ordered selections.\n\nThe excluded ordered numerators over 336 are: 444: 6; 445: 18; 443: 18; 442: 36; 441: 18; 225: 6; 224: 18; 223: 6; 221: 6. Their sum is 132. Hence the probability is\n$1-\\frac{132}{336}=\\frac{204}{336}=\\frac{17}{28}=0.607.$\n\n(M1): One correct unsimplified calculation for an identified scenario other than the three-4s case.\n\n(A1): Five correct probabilities evaluated. Accept unsimplified.\n\n(M1): Nine correct scenarios subtracted.\n\n(B1): 336 or $8\\times7\\times6$ used as the denominator.\n\n(A1): $17/28$ or 0.607.\n\nTotal 5.",
